{
  "id": "inflation_rate",
  "title": "Inflation Rate Calculator",
  "description": "Calculate the future value of money after periods with uniform or variable inflation rates. Understand how inflation erodes purchasing power over time.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Inflation Rate Calculator\n\nAn inflation with rising prices will decrease the value of money over time. A deflation - the opposite of inflation or negative inflation - with decreasing prices will increase the value of money over time.\n\n### Uniform Inflation Rate Formula\n\n**F = P(1 - i)^n**\n\nWhere:\n- **F** = Future value\n- **P** = Present value\n- **i** = Average inflation rate per period (positive for inflation, negative for deflation)\n- **n** = Number of periods"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "presentValue",
          "label": "Present Value (P)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 100,
          "unit": "$"
        },
        {
          "id": "inflationRate",
          "label": "Inflation Rate (i)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.04,
          "unit": "%"
        },
        {
          "id": "periods",
          "label": "Number of Periods (n)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "periods"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "futureValue",
          "label": "Future Value (F)",
          "formula": "inputs.presentValue * Math.pow((1 - inputs.inflationRate), inputs.periods)",
          "unit": "$",
          "format": "currency"
        },
        {
          "id": "purchasingPowerLoss",
          "label": "Purchasing Power Loss",
          "formula": "inputs.presentValue - (inputs.presentValue * Math.pow((1 - inputs.inflationRate), inputs.periods))",
          "unit": "$",
          "format": "currency"
        },
        {
          "id": "purchasingPowerLossPercent",
          "label": "Purchasing Power Loss (%)",
          "formula": "((inputs.presentValue - (inputs.presentValue * Math.pow((1 - inputs.inflationRate), inputs.periods))) / inputs.presentValue) * 100",
          "unit": "%",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}